---
number: 91
title: Oh, For a Thousand Tongues
author: Charles Wesley
composer: T. Jarman
sp_category: "7"
topic: Jesus’ Glory and Praise
notes: "AUTO: chorus detected heuristically — verify"
---

[verse 1]
Oh, for a thousand tongues to sing
My great Redeemer’s praise,
My great Redeemer’s praise.
The glories of my God and King.

[chorus]
The triumphs of His grace,
The triumphs of His grace,
The triumphs of His grace!

[verse 2]
My gracious Master and my God,
Assist me to proclaim,
To spread through all the earth abroad
The honors of Thy name, my God and King.

[chorus]
The triumphs of His grace,
The triumphs of His grace,
The triumphs of His grace!

[verse 3]
He breaks the cruel power of sin,
He sets the prisoner free;
His blood can make the foulest clean,
His blood avails for me, my God and King.

[chorus]
The triumphs of His grace,
The triumphs of His grace,
The triumphs of His grace!
